    "officialTopicCodes": true,
    "designNotes": "Units 1-3 only (Polynomial and Rational; Exponential and Logarithmic; Trigonometric and Polar), the units assessed on the exam. Unit 4 (Functions Involving Parameters, Vectors, and Matrices, 14 topics) is 'not assessed on the AP Exam' per the CED and is excluded; pacing is given in weeks, not class periods. Exam (read 2026-10-20, CED effective Fall 2026): 2 h 55 min; Section I 42 MC (62.5%): Part A 29 questions 65 min no calculator (43.75%), Part B 13 questions 40 min graphing calculator required (18.75%); Section II 4 FRQ, each 6 points, scored analytically, equal weight: Part A 2 questions 35 min graphing calculator required (FRQ 1 Function Concepts, FRQ 2 Modeling a Non-Periodic Context), Part B 2 questions 35 min no calculator (FRQ 3 Modeling a Periodic Context, FRQ 4 Symbolic Manipulations). Hybrid digital. Exam weighting for practices: Procedural and Symbolic Fluency 35-50%, Multiple Representations 20-30%, Communication and Reasoning 30-40% (whole-exam, not recorded as MC/FRQ-specific weights). MC function-type weights: general functions 15-25%, polynomial/rational 20-25%, exponential/logarithmic 20-30%, trigonometric/polar 30-35%. Topic titles of 1.2, 1.3, 1.8, 1.10, 1.12, 1.13, 2.1, 2.2, 2.4, 2.6, 2.8, 2.10, 2.13-2.15, 3.3, 3.7, 3.9, 3.13, 3.14 are not all verified word-for-word against the extracted text. Skills are the three mathematical practices at practice level. Per-topic and per-sub-keyword skills are an ALTON editorial mapping (one skill per sub-keyword chosen by kind and content), not the CED's per-topic suggested skills. Sub-keywords, kinds, requires and estLessons are ALTON editorial designs, not CED content. Topic titles are the CED's where read from the CED course-at-a-glance; where the extracted text was truncated they are close paraphrases."
